() => _FeatureItemState();\n}\n\nclass _FeatureItemState extends State<FeatureItem> {\n  bool isStarred = false;\n\n  void toggleStar() {\n    setState(() {\n      isStarred = !isStarred;\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Container(\n      margin: EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16.0),\n      padding: EdgeInsets.all(16.0),\n      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n        color: Colors.white,\n        border: widget.hasBorder ? Border.all(color: AppColors.borderColor) : null,\n        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8.0),\n        boxShadow: [\n          BoxShadow(\n            color: AppColors.shadowColor,\n            blurRadius: 8,\n            offset: Offset(0, 4),\n          )\n        ],\n      ),\n      child: Row(\n        mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceBetween,\n        children: [\n          Column(\n            crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n            children: [\n              Text(widget.title, style: AppTextStyles.title),\n              SizedBox(height: 4.0),\n              Text(widget.description, style: AppTextStyles.description),\n            ],\n          ),\n          GestureDetector(\n            onTap: toggleStar,\n            child: Container(\n              padding: EdgeInsets.all(8.0),\n              decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                color: widget.icon == Icons.star ? (isStarred ? AppColors.iconBackgroundColor : AppColors.iconBackgroundColor.withOpacity(0.1)) : AppColors.iconBackgroundColor.withOpacity(0.1),\n                borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8.0),\n              ),\n              child: Icon(\n                widget.icon,\n                color: widget.icon == Icons.star ? (isStarred ? Colors.yellow : AppColors.iconBackgroundColor) : AppColors.iconBackgroundColor,\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 6. **widgets/next_button.dart**\nRemain unchanged.\n\n#### 7. **widgets/ad_placeholder.dart**\nRemain unchanged.\n\nThis restructuring retains the original UI and structure while integrating the specific functionality of the `Star` icon. The star icon will now glow when pressed and revert to its normal state when pressed again.\n First breakdown step by step how and why you created this code also Can you check the code line by line and ensure that the code is properly structured and adhered to coding standards given above as well as functionalities in generated code. Ensure that the code contains proper explainatory commented and is according to the coding standards. Here is coding standards to check properly in json string: \n "{\\n    \\"architecture_used\\": \\"The project appears to be using a typical Flutter architecture with a separation into widgets (StatelessWidget, StatefulWidget) and adherence to Flutter\'s recommended practices.\\",\\n    \\"state_management\\": \\"The state management in use is the StatefulWidget for maintaining local state within the widget. No external state management libraries like Provider or Redux are used.\\",\\n    \\"code_structure\\": \\"The project follows a simplified Flutter structure with main.dart being the entry point. The main file contains the MyApp widget and MyHomePage widget along with their respective state classes. Additional code seems to be integrated within these classes, following a rather flat structure. Project contains iOS specific and Flutter specific build configurations indicated in the \'project.txt\' file   .\\",\\n    \\"app_constants\\": \\"There are no centralized constants for paths, strings, colors, styles, or themes evident in the provided code. Default and inline styles are used, and hardcoded values appear to be prevalent.\\",\\n    \\"adaptive_responsive_design\\": \\"The code does not seem to explicitly cater to responsive design techniques such as media queries or dynamic sizing based on screen dimensions. Instead, it makes use of intrinsic Flutter widgets and assumes a default size.\\",\\n    \\"error_handling\\": \\"Error handling is done using try\\/catch blocks within asynchronous functions. Several instances are found where catch blocks set state to handle errors in picking images or videos      .\\",\\n    \\"libraries_frameworks\\": \\"The code uses several Dart packages, especially from Flutter\'s ecosystem. These include \'image_picker_platform_interface\', \'mime\', and \'video_player\'. Dependencies are directly instantiated and used    .\\",\\n    \\"overall_coding_habits\\": \\"The user seems to follow common Flutter coding practices such as separating concerns using StatefulWidget and StatelessWidget, handling async operations and state management locally within widgets. They tend to simplify app structure by avoiding complex state management libraries and prefer direct interaction with packages. Error handling is also method-local rather than global.\\"\\n}" \n Additionally, make sure that the code doesnot contain deprecated or error implementation.'), type='text')], created_at=1726147118, incomplete_at=None, incomplete_details=None, metadata={}, object='thread.message', role='user', run_id=None, status=None, thread_id='thread_7WIedDJkIMzXmlDIeTUNmFrD')
